The filter: Use the 15-point checklist to identify sustainable growth engines

Red flags: Lack of management depth, poor labor relations, and lack of candor are dealbreakers

Expanded Insights:

Fisher provides a qualitative checklist—not quantitative metrics—for identifying truly exceptional companies

Price should not be the dominant factor; potential matters more

Point 2 (Future Innovation) distinguishes temporary growers from perpetual compounders

Point 7 (Labor Relations) predicts resilience during talent shortages

Point 9 (Management Depth) determines whether the company survives its founder

Mentor's Takeaway: I've printed this checklist and used it for every major investment I've made in the past two decades. Point 15 is the gatekeeper—if integrity is absent, I don't even bother with the other fourteen.

