Original Summary:

Don't over-diversify. 10 to 15 deeply researched names beat 50 mediocre ones

Don't panic over geopolitical war scares (often great buying opportunities)

Don't anchor your expectations to past stock prices

Don't lose patience if the market takes time to recognize fundamental execution

Don't blindly follow the crowd or financial media

Expanded Insights:
These additional don'ts address portfolio construction, psychological biases, and information sources.

Mentor's Takeaway: The investors I've seen succeed over decades all share Fisher's traits: curiosity about businesses, patience to wait for the right opportunities, and discipline to hold when others panic.

Agent Implementation ODC:

Limit portfolio to 10-20 companies maximum (fewer if smaller portfolio)

During geopolitical crises, review holdings against 15-point checklist. If still passing, consider adding

