Part II: Conservative Investors Sleep Well
Fisher's later work addresses what makes an investment truly conservative—safe enough that even conservative investors can sleep soundly.

The Four Dimensions of a Conservative Investment:

Dimension	Description
1. Superiority in Operations	Low-cost production, strong marketing, effective R&D, sound financial management
2. The People Factor	Orientation toward people, management depth, integrity at all levels
3. Investment Characteristics	Defensible competitive positions, pricing power, customer loyalty
4. Price	Even the best company is a poor investment at too high a price
Mentor's Takeaway: These dimensions create a framework for evaluating safety. True safety comes from business quality, not statistical measures. The companies that let me sleep best during the 2008 crisis were precisely those Fisher would identify through these four dimensions.

Agent Implementation ODC:

Evaluate every holding against the four dimensions annually

Flag any company weakening on dimensions 1-3 regardless of stock price

Dimension 4 (price) matters at purchase; dimensions 1-3 matter forever

"Sleep well" test: If you can't sleep due to worry about a holding, investigate immediately

